  "title": "Iran Financial Pressure and Banking-System Isolation",
  "question": "What legal, licensing, designation and operating states did Operation Economic Outcast change, and which announced financial-institution, branch, SWIFT/dollar, crypto and domestic-banking outcomes remain unproven?",
  "bluf": "Treasury's August 28 Operation Economic Outcast receipt partly resolves the forecast: FinCEN proposed, but did not yet impose, Section 311 Special Measure Five against Banque Misr UAE, while OFAC separately designated Reza Jalali Taeedi and Kameng Maritime Limited. The proposal would prohibit covered U.S. institutions from opening or maintaining correspondent accounts for or on behalf of the named UAE bank if finalized. It does not establish an operative ban, closure of a named account, failed payment, universal SWIFT or dollar exclusion, domestic Iranian banking shutdown, asset seizure, or any Federal Reserve or IMF change.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-09-03T19:41:23-04:00",
  "evidence_cutoff_note": "Targeted refresh through September 3 covers Treasury's August 28 release and the September 1 Federal Register publication; the rest of the package retains its stated cutoffs.",
  "use_note": "Supports the August 24 legal and licensing state plus the September 3 Banque Misr UAE proposal and separate OFAC designations. It does not establish a final or effective Section 311 prohibition, named account closure, payment failure, universal SWIFT or dollar exclusion, asset seizure or domestic banking shutdown.",
